==Trivia==
*"Kamisama Kōrin" was originally "[https://youtu.be/GXFSK0ogeg4 O Fortuna ~ Carmina Burana]", an orchestral suite, changed later presumably for copyright concerns.
*"Apollo Kessen" is named after [[wikipedia:Apollo 11|Apollo 11]], the spaceflight mission that landed humans on the [[Moon (Into the Future)|Moon]] for the first time.
*The Filibuster Invasion theme sounds similar to "[https://youtu.be/51yni6pCXM8 Megalomania]" from the SNES game [[wikipedia:Live A Live|''Live A Live'']].
*The River City Stages' theme is a remix of [[wikipedia:Csikós Post|Csikós Post]], which can be heard in a variety of other games ranging from [[wikipedia:Yoshi's Cookie|''Yoshi's Cookie'']] to [[wikipedia:Hamtaro: Ham-Hams Unite!|''Hamtaro: Ham-Hams Unite!'']].
*The New Year's Bling theme is [[wikipedia:Haru no Umi|''Haru no Umi'']], a piece by [[wikipedia:Michio Miyagi|Michio Miyagi]] associated with the Japanese New Year.
*Underground Labyrinth Theme #1 sounds similar to "[https://youtu.be/USlwK2QHz_0 Monsters in the Dungeon]" (also known as "Deep Underground") from the ''[https://dragon-quest.org/wiki/Dragon_Quest_V:_Hand_of_the_Heavenly_Bride Dragon Quest V]'' soundtrack.
*Zero Legends Theme #4 contains the leitmotifs of "World Invasion", "Minzoku Dai Idō" and "Lunar Battle", which the first three Zero Legends themes were remixes of. A comparison can be found [https://youtu.be/_PgaLrxla0c here].
*Zero Legends Theme #5 sounds similar to the [https://youtu.be/HqC-wWqv_oQ&list=PL6m622N0YaXKd0tFARiWbTARM21DYyLM8&index=6 original version] of "Beasts that Shake the Earth" from [[Ganso!! Nyanko Daisensou]] and [[Kumanchu Royale]].
*[[Nyanko New Japan]]'s title theme is a remix of ''[[wikipedia:L'Arlésienne (Bizet)#4. Farandole|Farandole]]''.
*Nyanko New Japan's gameplay theme is a remix of the ''[[wikipedia:Symphony No. 9 (Dvořák)|New World Symphony]]''.
*Uncanny Legends Theme #2 was added in [[Version 7.0 Update|Version 7.0]], but was unimplemented until [[Version 7.1 Update|Version 7.1]].
*snd147 was a duplicate of snd036 and had been reserved as a placeholder from [[Version 11.6 Update|Version 11.6]] to [[Version 12.0 Update|Version 12.0]], when it was implemented and used in [[Revival of Origin]].

